  "term": "warm-up",
  "definition": "A warm-up is a set of preparatory activities done before a main physical task to influence immediate movement and muscle performance. In this source, it includes an initial standardized treadmill activity followed by methods such as dynamic stretching, foam rolling, or resistance-band exercises, which can affect force, power, or timing in different ways.",
